What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/hw_ldac_tg_state
KernelVersion:	6.13
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Controls the static signal level on the LDAC/TGP/DCK pin. The
		active function of this pin depends on the DAC operating mode.
		Valid values are:
		- "low": pin driven low (0% duty cycle)
		- "high": pin driven high (100% duty cycle)

		Setting this overrides hw_ldac_tg_pwm.

		Requires optional PWM device tree configuration.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/hw_ldac_tg_state_available
KernelVersion:	6.13
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Returns the available LDAC GPIO states: "low high"

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/hw_ldac_tg_pwm
KernelVersion:	6.13
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Enable or disable 50% duty cycle PWM on the LDAC/TGP/DCK pin.
		The active function of this pin depends on the DAC operating mode.
		Valid values are:
		- "disable": PWM disabled, pin returns to hw_ldac_tg_state level
		- "enable": PWM enabled with 50% duty cycle

		The PWM frequency is set via sampling_frequency. Valid range is
		1 kHz to 10 MHz. Default is 1 MHz.

		Requires optional PWM device tree configuration.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/hw_ldac_tg_pwm_available
KernelVersion:	6.13
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Returns the available PWM states: "disable enable"

